>> title: Memphis Dry Rub
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: barbecue, pork, ribs, spice blend, pantry
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: dry rub, rub, Memphis rub, rib rub
>> pairs-with: barbecue-sauce, boston-baked-beans
>> servings: 12
>> time: 10 min
>> step.1: rub the lumps out
>> step.2: whisk in
>> step.3: whisk in
>> step.4: crumble in

Rub @sweet paprika{1/4%cup}(28 g) and @dark brown sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g) together between your fingers until no lumps are left.

Whisk @kosher salt{2%Tbs}, @black pepper{1%Tbs}, @cayenne{2%tsp}, and @dry mustard{1%tsp} into @&(~1)paprika base{}.

Whisk @garlic powder{1%Tbs}, @onion powder{1%Tbs}, and @celery seed{1%tsp} into @&(~1)mixture{}.

Crumble @dried oregano{2%tsp} and @dried thyme{1%tsp} between your palms into @&(~1)rub{}.
